+/* dkr360: the PT-BR translation (Dream64) keeps the texts that the C code hardcodes (credits titles, place
+ * ordinals, "CAN'T SAVE GHOST", RACE/LAP...) in its own copy of the game code, which Golden Balloon does not
+ * run. So when the loaded ROM is that translation, those literals are swapped at draw time (font.c). The
+ * punctuation inside the Portuguese strings ($ @ ) ( < & *) is that translation's own accent-glyph encoding. */
